@startuml
title HAP - Security (OAuth2/JWT + mTLS) - TARGET P3

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

actor "User (Paciente/Médico/Admin)" as User

package "Kubernetes Cluster" as K8S {

  [Nginx Ingress (TLS)] as Ingress

  package "Microservices" as MS {
    component "auth-service\n(OAuth2/JWT issuer)" as Auth
    component "clients-service\n(Resource Server)" as Clients
    component "doctors-service\n(Resource Server)" as Doctors
    component "appointments-service\n(Resource Server)" as Appointments
    component "notes-service\n(Resource Server)" as Notes
  }

  queue "RabbitMQ (AMQP)" as MQ

  component "Certificate Authority / cert-manager\n(Issues service certs)" as CA
}

' --- External user authentication/authorization (OAuth2/JWT) ---
User --> Ingress : HTTPS (public)

User --> Auth : POST /auth/login\n(credentials)
Auth --> User : JWT access token (+ refresh token optional)

User --> Ingress : HTTPS + Authorization: Bearer JWT
Ingress --> Appointments : forward request + JWT

Appointments --> Appointments : validate JWT (signature, exp)\n+ roles/scopes
Clients --> Clients : validate JWT (signature, exp)\n+ roles/scopes
Doctors --> Doctors : validate JWT (signature, exp)\n+ roles/scopes
Notes --> Notes : validate JWT (signature, exp)\n+ roles/scopes

' --- Internal service-to-service (mTLS) ---
CA --> MS : issue service certificates\n(auth, clients, doctors, appointments, notes)

Appointments -[#blue]-> Clients : REST internal call\nmTLS (client cert + server cert)
Appointments -[#blue]-> Doctors : REST internal call\nmTLS (client cert + server cert)
Appointments -[#blue]-> Notes : (optional) internal call\nmTLS

' --- RabbitMQ security (optional but strong for P3) ---
MS -[#blue]-> MQ : AMQP over TLS\n(optional client cert)
MQ -[#blue]-> MS : AMQP over TLS

note right of Ingress
External traffic:
- TLS termination at Ingress
- JWT passed to services
- Services enforce roles/scopes on endpoints
end note

note right of Appointments
Zero-trust internal:
- every service call is authenticated (mTLS)
- authorization still enforced per endpoint
end note

@enduml
